1. Nature of this license
   This project is private and is NOT open source. Nothing in this document grants
   anyone the right to copy, distribute or sell the project. Every right not expressly
   granted here is reserved by the project owner.

2. What "the Project" means
   Everything created specifically for the "Molook Al Tarneeb" website: the source
   code (client, server, game engine, tests, build scripts), the visual design, the
   icons and graphics drawn inside the project, the Arabic and English texts, and the
   documentation. Third-party components described in section 7 are excluded.

3. Not permitted without the owner's prior written permission
   a. Copying the Project or any substantial part of it, publishing it, or uploading it
      to a public repository or hosting service.
   b. Distributing or redistributing it, in whole or in part, modified or unmodified.
   c. Selling, reselling, renting or sublicensing it, or bundling it into a paid
      product or service.
   d. Running a copy on a server to make it available to others as a service, whether
      free of charge or for a fee.
   e. Creating derivative works from it, or using its name, visual identity or texts in
      another project.
   f. Removing or altering copyright notices, the owner's name, or this license.

4. What is permitted
   a. The project owner, and anyone to whom the owner grants express written
      permission, within the limits of that permission.
   b. Visitors to the website as officially published by the owner may play on it free
      of charge in a web browser. This is use of a service, not a license to the source
      code or assets.
   c. Personal, non-commercial reading of files that the owner has handed to them,
      without copying or distributing them beyond what section 3 allows.

5. Requesting permission
   Written permission must be requested from the project owner directly. This document
   deliberately includes no contact details; refer to the project owner for any request.

6. Disclaimer
   The Project is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
   including fitness for a particular purpose or freedom from errors. To the extent
   permitted by applicable law, the owner is not liable for any damage arising from the
   use of, or inability to use, the Project.

7. Third-party components
   The Project uses open-source software libraries that belong to their authors and are
   governed by their own licenses (for example React, ws and zod). This license does
   not change the terms of those libraries or transfer their ownership. They are listed
   in OWNERSHIP.md, and their license texts are bundled in
   dist/public/third-party-licenses.txt after running the build command. The card game
   Tarneeb itself is a traditional game whose rules are owned by no one; this license
   covers the specific implementation, design and texts of the Project, not the rules of
   the game.

8. Language
   This license is written in Arabic and English. If the two differ in meaning, the
   Arabic text prevails.
